From 7c9cd8c1be22cc93ca92b974f2ac9676e4cf5444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kauan Turcato Storto <159664484+KauanDev1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:42:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat: translate for an emulated Xenos GPU under
 LR_LEGACYRECOMP

With LR_LEGACYRECOMP the translator targets LegacyRecomp's emulated GPU,
which knows Xenos registers, not D3D constant names:

- float constants by register index from the stage buffer (BDA, unchanged
  push constants), with relative addressing for any constant and literals
  from the definition table as locals;
- 128 boolean constants per stage (cond_exec, cond_exec_pred and cond_jmp,
  all honoured; upstream ignored the cond_exec conditions) and 32 loop
  constants (count, start and step; nested aL restored) in the shared block;
- texture and sampler heap indices per texture fetch constant (0..31);
- vertex inputs: vertex element i of the container is input location i
  (float4), with its vertex fetch slot, offset, stride and format recorded
  for the runtime; no usage location table;
- alpha test with all eight Xenos compare functions via spec constant 0
  (enable bit 1, function in bits 2..4); g_HalfPixelOffset kept;
- r0.x starts as the vertex index; oPos is zeroed; point-size exports go to
  a local;
- the microcode hash (XXH3-64 of the big-endian microcode) is computed and
  every table read is bounds-checked: malformed containers and unsupported
  constructs throw LrTranslationError instead of asserting;
- the Unleashed Recompiled specifics (usage location table, swapped
  texcoords, R11G11B10 normals, bicubic GI, alpha to coverage, reverse Z)
  are compiled out, and UNLEASHED_RECOMP together with LR_LEGACYRECOMP is
  an error.

The layout is in the LR_* macros of shader_common.h. Without
LR_LEGACYRECOMP nothing changes.

LegacyRecomp patch; same license as XenosRecomp (MIT).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
